;; This repository is a Guix channel: (rpi kernel) and (rpi firmware) are
;; modules you import, with no -L plumbing and no file copying.
;;
;; THE DEPENDENCY IS NOT OPTIONAL. Those modules import (nongnu packages linux)
;; — linux-firmware, which carries the radio firmware — so the channel cannot be
;; COMPILED without nonguix in the graph. Declaring it here means `guix pull' and
;; `guix time-machine' fetch it at this exact commit; a channel whose modules
;; import an undeclared channel fails during the checkout with
;; "no code for module (nongnu packages linux)".
;;
;; Written as DATA, not as a (make-channel-introduction …) call: a dependency is
;; read with `read' and parsed by `sexp->channel-introduction', which accepts
;; only this shape. A call form stops guix with "channel dependency has an
;; invalid introduction field", and a quoted name fails on symbol->string.
(channel
 (version 0)
 (dependencies
  (channel
   (name nonguix)
   (url "https://gitlab.com/nonguix/nonguix.git")
   (branch "master")
   (commit "6c2d4c89947e4fa381c896a204ee6bc5e81a7b8d")
   (introduction
    (channel-introduction
     (version 0)
     (commit "897c1a470da759236cc11798f4e0a5f7d4d59fbc")
     (signer "2A39 3FFF 68F4 EF7A 3D29  12AF 6F51 20A0 22FB B2D5"))))))
